<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<project xmlns="http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
    xsi:schemaLocation="http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0 https://maven.apache.org/xsd/maven-4.0.0.xsd">
    <modelVersion>4.0.0</modelVersion>

    <groupId>ai.proxyma</groupId>
    <artifactId>proxyma-monorepo</artifactId>
    <version>1.0.0</version>
    <packaging>pom</packaging>
    <name>proxyma-monorepo</name>
    <description>Aggregator for every Java module in the repository</description>

    <!--
      AGGREGATOR ONLY - deliberately not a parent.

      Each module keeps spring-boot-starter-parent as its parent and keeps its own version
      (app 0.36.0, license 1.0.0, telemetry 1.0.0, shared-contracts 1.3.0). Making this a parent
      would force one version onto four things that release independently, which is not what the
      merge was for: one repository, still four release cycles.

      What it IS for: putting shared-contracts in the same reactor as its three consumers, so
      `mvn -pl :proxyma-license -am package` builds the DTOs FROM SOURCE instead of resolving
      them from GitHub Packages. That retires the 401 that came back four different ways: no
      token, expired token, missing read:packages, and a version that was never published, all
      of which Maven surfaced identically.

      The friction it removes was never protecting what it appeared to. A desktop client in the
      field carries whatever contracts version it shipped with, so client and services have
      always been able to differ; compile-time coupling in CI never changed that. What does
      protect against skew is the rule, now in .claude/rules/backend-maven.md: adding an optional
      field is safe, renaming or removing one breaks whichever side deploys second.

      NOTE: a version pin must match the module for the reactor to substitute it. Merging the
      repos exposed that proxyma-license still pinned contracts 1.1.0 while the source had moved
      to 1.2.0 - invisible while each repo resolved its own copy from Packages.

      proxyma-desktop is a module of apps/app/backend/pom.xml - the COMMUNITY reactor. Proxyma
      Enterprise (proxyma-server and the modules only it carries) is ee/, which joins under the
      `server` profile below and nowhere else.
    -->
    <modules>
        <module>libs/shared-contracts</module>
        <module>apps/app/backend</module>
    </modules>

    <profiles>
        <!-- PROXYMA ENTERPRISE. `-Pserver` adds ee/ (closed source, never exported - see
             docs/architecture.html#oss-boundary). Explicit rather than activated by the directory's presence, so a
             desktop build in the private repository does not compile Enterprise too. A checkout
             without ee/ - the public Community repository - never passes it. -->
        <profile>
            <id>server</id>
            <modules>
                <module>ee</module>
            </modules>
        </profile>
        <!-- The operator services: the license server and the telemetry server. Private, and absent
             from the public Community repository, so each joins the reactor only when its directory
             is there - which in this repository is always, so `mvn -pl :proxyma-license -am` works as
             it always has. -->
        <profile>
            <id>license-server</id>
            <activation>
                <file><exists>${basedir}/apps/license/backend/pom.xml</exists></file>
            </activation>
            <modules>
                <module>apps/license/backend</module>
            </modules>
        </profile>
        <profile>
            <id>telemetry-server</id>
            <activation>
                <file><exists>${basedir}/apps/telemetry/backend/pom.xml</exists></file>
            </activation>
            <modules>
                <module>apps/telemetry/backend</module>
            </modules>
        </profile>
    </profiles>

</project>
